          "guid": "mt15fyf4lwx2xhuv",
          "message": {
            "text": "The remaining claim is blocked by observability, not by a newly proven font mismatch. Paths mode erases face provenance into global gN identifiers, embedded diagnostics are aggregate-only, and raw text fallback performs an unowned second font selection in the consumer; DM-2398 and DM-2399 isolate those risks.",
            "markdown": "The remaining claim is blocked by observability, not by a newly proven font mismatch. Paths mode erases face provenance into global gN identifiers, embedded diagnostics are aggregate-only, and raw text fallback performs an unowned second font selection in the consumer; DM-2398 and DM-2399 isolate those risks."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/142-renderer-font-route-audit.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 59,
                  "endLine": 70,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "4. **Current artifacts cannot prove the end-to-end claim.** Paths mode loses\n   face provenance when glyph definitions receive global `gN` IDs. Embedded\n   mode reports aggregate builder provenance only after a successful build.\n   Neither records why the shaped splitter declined, why embedded mode fell\n   back, or which source span used which mechanism.\n5. **No new production face divergence was proven by static/source audit.** The\n   unresolved issue is observability, not evidence that a particular current\n   run is wrong. DM-2398 must add a renderer ledger and join it to the unified\n   Chromium evidence before this area can claim exact end-to-end coverage.\n6. **Raw `<text>` fallback is a separate correctness risk.** It delegates a\n   second face-selection pass to the SVG consumer, which need not have the\n   capture host's font inventory or fallback rules. DM-2399 isolates that work."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
